'<p class="l-text"><strong>Linear algebra</strong> is the mathematical backbone of machine learning, computer graphics, and scientific computing. NumPy\'s <code>np.linalg</code> module gives you production-ready implementations of matrix operations, decompositions, and solvers \u2014 all backed by LAPACK and BLAS, the same battle-tested Fortran libraries used in MATLAB and R. In this lesson, you will learn to multiply matrices, solve linear systems, decompose matrices, and measure distances \u2014 all without a single Python loop.</p>'

